{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider-64 send 0xa5 fails with TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5, i.e. RX saw idle 0xff instead of data. Root cause is TX reset send_pattern <= ~1 (LSB 0 break) instead of ~0 idle-high, driving ser_tx low through reset and causing a false start that fills RX with 0xff before real data. Provenance picosoc/picosoc.v:190 simpleuart instance and picosoc/simpleuart.v:20 module pins this to TX reset logic.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -113,5 +113,5 @@
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			send_dummy <= 1;", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: uart data mismatch, uart loopback 0xa5 matches"}

